WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.535
-Our next guest
is a writer and actor

00:00:02.535 --> 00:00:04.604
who recently won an Emmy
for his portrayal or Roy Kent

00:00:04.604 --> 00:00:06.739
on the critically acclaimed
series "Ted Lasso."

00:00:06.739 --> 00:00:09.141
The second season finale
is available to stream

00:00:09.141 --> 00:00:11.177
this Friday on Apple TV+.

00:00:11.177 --> 00:00:12.478
Let's take a look.

00:00:12.478 --> 00:00:15.415
-Big man Roy Kent.
-No.

00:00:15.415 --> 00:00:17.083
-Come on, man.
Why won't you coach me?

00:00:17.083 --> 00:00:18.484
-'Cause you don't deserve it.

00:00:18.484 --> 00:00:20.019
-You're right.
I don't deserve it.

00:00:20.019 --> 00:00:22.355
-And the way you play
is dull and conformist.

00:00:22.355 --> 00:00:26.826
-It's true. I do play in quite
a dull and conformist way.

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:36.136
-And you're ugly.

00:00:38.871 --> 00:00:42.742
You're an ugly, ugly boy.

00:00:42.742 --> 00:00:46.146
With bad hair.
-[ Scoffs ]

00:00:50.249 --> 00:00:51.784
-Say it.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:51.784 --> 00:00:54.086
-Please welcome to the show
Brett Goldstein.

00:00:54.086 --> 00:00:56.589 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:56.589 --> 00:00:57.657
-Hey.
-Hey.

00:00:57.657 --> 00:00:59.692
-Welcome. See?
This is real Edinburgh --

00:00:59.692 --> 00:01:02.428
first Edinburgh show energy.
-Yeah, hey.

00:01:02.428 --> 00:01:04.997
Hi. Yeah.
[ Applause ]

00:01:04.997 --> 00:01:06.633
Thank you.

00:01:06.633 --> 00:01:08.767
-I am thrilled you're here.

00:01:08.767 --> 00:01:10.870
-I'm delighted to be here.
Thank you for having me.

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:14.040
-Such a fan of your work, and
to meet you in person is great.

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:16.375
And, you know,
I hope everybody knows

00:01:16.375 --> 00:01:18.778
at this point that you're also
a writer on the show.

00:01:18.778 --> 00:01:20.747
-Yes.
-And it seemed like that --

00:01:20.747 --> 00:01:23.583
it just must be so much fun
to be in the writers room,

00:01:23.583 --> 00:01:25.852
first, writing something
so funny,

00:01:25.852 --> 00:01:28.554
knowing that you then get to be
the person who performs it.

00:01:28.554 --> 00:01:31.825
-I mean, I did write that scene,
and the problem is,

00:01:31.825 --> 00:01:33.259
I knew as I was writing it,

00:01:33.259 --> 00:01:34.827
this is gonna cost Apple
a lot of money,

00:01:34.827 --> 00:01:38.164
because I can't do scenes
with Phil Dunster,

00:01:38.164 --> 00:01:41.067
who plays Jamie Tartt,
without losing my [bleep].

00:01:41.067 --> 00:01:43.636
And as I was writing,
"You're an ugly, ugly boy,"

00:01:43.636 --> 00:01:45.705
I thought,
"This is gonna take days."

00:01:45.705 --> 00:01:47.139
[ Laughter ]

00:01:47.139 --> 00:01:48.741
"This is gonna
take days to shoot."

00:01:48.741 --> 00:01:52.411
You may notice there were less
Roy-Jamie scenes this season,

00:01:52.411 --> 00:01:53.779
and that was purely
to save money.

00:01:53.779 --> 00:01:55.347
-Just to save money.
They can't have you guys

00:01:55.347 --> 00:01:56.983
in a two-shot together.
-Yeah.

00:01:56.983 --> 00:01:58.318
-They got a lot of
over-the-shoulders.

00:01:58.318 --> 00:02:00.119
-Yeah.
[ Both laugh ]

00:02:00.119 --> 00:02:02.021
-So, congratulations
on your Emmy.

00:02:02.021 --> 00:02:04.858
-Thank you very much.
-You cursed when you won...

00:02:04.858 --> 00:02:06.225
-Yeah.
-...in your acceptance speech.

00:02:06.225 --> 00:02:08.294
-Proud of it.
-As you should be.

00:02:08.294 --> 00:02:09.661
It's what the fans want.
-Yeah.

00:02:09.661 --> 00:02:10.830
-You know what I mean?

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:12.198
It's what the people
who voted for you wanted.

00:02:12.198 --> 00:02:13.833
-They told me not to.
-They did.

00:02:13.833 --> 00:02:15.201
-Repeatedly.
And I kept thinking --

00:02:15.201 --> 00:02:17.303
-So in the run up, they were
afraid this might happen?

00:02:17.303 --> 00:02:20.673
-A few people said,
"If you win, don't swear."

00:02:20.673 --> 00:02:22.308
And I was like,
"Why are you saying this?

00:02:22.308 --> 00:02:24.376
Like, now I'm gonna
do it twice."

00:02:24.376 --> 00:02:26.012
You know what I mean?
[ Laughter ]

00:02:26.012 --> 00:02:27.446
And the more you say it,
the more --

00:02:27.446 --> 00:02:28.981
I mean, if they kept saying it,

00:02:28.981 --> 00:02:31.184
the speech would've
just been [bleep].

00:02:31.184 --> 00:02:33.118
[ Laughter ]
Like...

00:02:33.118 --> 00:02:35.955
But, you know, it was --
Can I tell you this?

00:02:35.955 --> 00:02:38.791
People keep saying to me,
"What was winning an Emmy like?"

00:02:38.791 --> 00:02:40.259
What it was actually like --

00:02:40.259 --> 00:02:43.729
It was very early in the show,
and we'd sat -- we were late.

00:02:43.729 --> 00:02:47.566
We were stuck in a queue.
I've never been to such a thing.

00:02:47.566 --> 00:02:49.802
And we're stuck in the queue
with lots of famous people.

00:02:49.802 --> 00:02:51.671
You're like, "Oh, famous people
have to queue, as well."

00:02:51.671 --> 00:02:54.773
And they're, like, queued,
and then suddenly we were told,

00:02:54.773 --> 00:02:56.709
"You don't have time
to do a red carpet.

00:02:56.709 --> 00:02:58.244
You've got to come
because the show started."

00:02:58.244 --> 00:03:00.413
And we sat down, and it was all,
like, "Oh, what's this?"

00:03:00.413 --> 00:03:03.116
and then suddenly, it started.

00:03:03.116 --> 00:03:04.783
Cedric the Entertainer
and a load of people

00:03:04.783 --> 00:03:06.819
started singing and dancing
towards us.

00:03:06.819 --> 00:03:08.688
And everyone stood up,
and all I was thinking was,

00:03:08.688 --> 00:03:10.523
"Oh [bleep]
Have I got a dance?"

00:03:10.523 --> 00:03:13.593
[ Laughter ]
Like, "What is this?"

00:03:13.593 --> 00:03:15.728
And then everyone said --
I was like, "Oh [bleep]"

00:03:15.728 --> 00:03:16.996
I couldn't see
where the cameras were.

00:03:16.996 --> 00:03:18.764
I was thinking,
"Please, don't make me a meme."

00:03:18.764 --> 00:03:20.766
Like, "What is this?"
[ Laughter ]

00:03:20.766 --> 00:03:22.001
I was just so embarrassed.

00:03:22.001 --> 00:03:24.136
Like, no one told me
there'd be dancing.

00:03:24.136 --> 00:03:27.406
And then I won an Emmy.
So, like, I was in no --

00:03:27.406 --> 00:03:29.174
I was just spending
the whole time thinking...

00:03:29.174 --> 00:03:31.277
-And so even when you were
giving your acceptance speech,

00:03:31.277 --> 00:03:32.478
was part of you still worried

00:03:32.478 --> 00:03:34.280
that you got caught on camera
dancing badly?

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:36.482
-Yeah, just, like,
looking horrified.

00:03:36.482 --> 00:03:38.351
[ Laughter ]

00:03:38.351 --> 00:03:41.053
-What is it like now --
especially as you --

00:03:41.053 --> 00:03:43.155
I know you guys are working
now on season three.

00:03:43.155 --> 00:03:46.425
-Yeah.
-How protective are you

00:03:46.425 --> 00:03:50.663
of Roy Kent, being the person
who also plays Roy Kent?

00:03:50.663 --> 00:03:54.334
-The truth is,
I try, in the writers room,

00:03:54.334 --> 00:03:56.402
not to pitch a lot of Roy stuff,

00:03:56.402 --> 00:03:58.070
'cause I love
all the characters equally.

00:03:58.070 --> 00:03:59.505
-[ Laughing ] Uh-huh.

00:03:59.505 --> 00:04:01.741
-But...
[ Laughter ]

00:04:01.741 --> 00:04:03.443
No, they're all my children.

00:04:03.443 --> 00:04:05.177
You know,
I don't have a favorite.

00:04:05.177 --> 00:04:08.347
But sometimes
I do find myself going,

00:04:08.347 --> 00:04:11.550
"Roy wouldn't [bleep] say that."
[ Laughter ]

00:04:11.550 --> 00:04:13.852
And now I have an Emmy.
Like, "Oh, yeah!"

00:04:13.852 --> 00:04:15.554
[ Laughter ]
-So, you bring it.

00:04:15.554 --> 00:04:18.057
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
-Obviously, you would.

00:04:18.057 --> 00:04:19.458
I think that
one of the things --

00:04:19.458 --> 00:04:22.662
the journey, Roy's journey,
that we all enjoyed so much

00:04:22.662 --> 00:04:24.530
was this incredibly
gruff character.

00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:26.432
And, especially in season two,

00:04:26.432 --> 00:04:29.234
you see this really sweet side
of him, as well.

00:04:29.234 --> 00:04:31.737
You know, obviously you guys put
a lot of care into that arc.

00:04:31.737 --> 00:04:33.506
But that must be
a fun part of it, as well.

00:04:33.506 --> 00:04:35.541
You're not paying someone
who's one-dimensional.

00:04:35.541 --> 00:04:37.376
-No, I mean, all the characters,

00:04:37.376 --> 00:04:41.480
most of our time in the writers
room is spent discussing --

00:04:41.480 --> 00:04:42.948
Like, I think the aim of
"Ted Lasso,"

00:04:42.948 --> 00:04:46.285
all the characters have --
they start off, you hate them,

00:04:46.285 --> 00:04:48.720
and in the end,
we'll make you like them.

00:04:48.720 --> 00:04:50.489
Because everyone
has their reasons.

00:04:50.489 --> 00:04:53.325
You know what I mean?
[ Laughter ]

00:04:53.325 --> 00:04:57.596
Everyone you hate has a reason
that they're a dick.

00:04:57.596 --> 00:04:59.098
You know what I mean?
Like...

00:04:59.098 --> 00:05:02.402
Some people, it's very hard
to find that reason,

00:05:02.402 --> 00:05:05.071
and that's the real challenge.
-Yeah.

00:05:05.071 --> 00:05:06.405
I feel like you made it
particularly hard

00:05:06.405 --> 00:05:07.406
on your friend Phil.

00:05:07.406 --> 00:05:08.807
You've given him
the hardest journey.

00:05:08.807 --> 00:05:10.776
-Yeah.
-[ Laughs ]

00:05:10.776 --> 00:05:13.245
-I stand by it.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:13.245 --> 00:05:15.681
He'll be fine.
-So, we were talking backstage.

00:05:15.681 --> 00:05:18.117
Brendan Hunt,
who plays Coach Beard, he and I,

00:05:18.117 --> 00:05:20.152
and Jason, and Joe Kelly,
we were all in Amsterdam

00:05:20.152 --> 00:05:21.453
around the same time.
-Yeah.

00:05:21.453 --> 00:05:23.789
-We all fell in love
with soccer at the same time.

00:05:23.789 --> 00:05:25.191
I apologize that I'm not
calling it football,

00:05:25.191 --> 00:05:26.692
but, of course,
we have a football here,

00:05:26.692 --> 00:05:29.695
a football that you are not --
you're not falling in love with

00:05:29.695 --> 00:05:32.598
the same way that Brendan and I
fell in love with your football.

00:05:32.598 --> 00:05:35.968
-I feel like anyone --
You're all gonna hate me now.

00:05:35.968 --> 00:05:39.939
Hey, you call it football,
but you use your hands.

00:05:39.939 --> 00:05:42.275
-Yeah.
-So, exhibit A,

00:05:42.275 --> 00:05:44.677
what are you doing?
[ Laughter ]

00:05:44.677 --> 00:05:46.879
B, what the [bleep]
is going on?

00:05:46.879 --> 00:05:49.749
I've watched
the Super Bowl five times.

00:05:49.749 --> 00:05:52.418
It stops every three seconds.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:52.418 --> 00:05:54.887
Then there's an advert,
then something happens,

00:05:54.887 --> 00:05:57.757
then there's a chap and mics,
people talking.

00:05:57.757 --> 00:06:00.359
Like, just [bleep] play this.
What's going on?

00:06:00.359 --> 00:06:02.328
[ Laughter ]
And I'm like,

00:06:02.328 --> 00:06:04.463
"Americans must be genius
because I've watched it --

00:06:04.463 --> 00:06:06.432
I still have no idea
what is happening."

00:06:06.432 --> 00:06:08.967
It looks like everyone
has worked out a lot,

00:06:08.967 --> 00:06:12.572
and good luck to them,
but, like, what is the sport?

00:06:12.572 --> 00:06:13.872
And then I went
to a baseball game,

00:06:13.872 --> 00:06:15.975
and I love baseball
because of the baseball films.

00:06:15.975 --> 00:06:17.276
-Yeah.
-What I realized is,

00:06:17.276 --> 00:06:20.479
in baseball films,
they cut out all the game shows

00:06:20.479 --> 00:06:22.548
and the adverts.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:22.548 --> 00:06:23.849
Like, there's an advert
every minute.

00:06:23.849 --> 00:06:26.552
People brought on the field
to fire a T-shirt at you.

00:06:26.552 --> 00:06:28.687
And then the worst thing
with all American sports is,

00:06:28.687 --> 00:06:31.157
at some point -- at any point,
you're in danger of being

00:06:31.157 --> 00:06:32.792
put on camera,
and you have to get off

00:06:32.792 --> 00:06:35.528
with the person next to you.
Like, it's not safe.

00:06:35.528 --> 00:06:37.396
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, that's true.

00:06:37.396 --> 00:06:39.131
-In a time of #MeToo,
we shouldn't be having

00:06:39.131 --> 00:06:41.567
[bleep] kiss cams.
"Now I've got to..."

00:06:41.567 --> 00:06:43.202
-These are all
very good arguments.

00:06:43.202 --> 00:06:44.803
It's very hard to defend.
-I'm sorry.

00:06:44.803 --> 00:06:46.972
But, listen, I'm sure
something's going on.

00:06:46.972 --> 00:06:48.140
I just...
-Yeah.

00:06:48.140 --> 00:06:50.275
-...don't get it.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:50.275 --> 00:06:53.345
-So, I think everybody
would just feel very confident

00:06:53.345 --> 00:06:55.514
in assuming that the best work
you've done over the past

00:06:55.514 --> 00:06:57.783
two years is "Ted Lasso."

00:06:57.783 --> 00:07:00.185
But you would disabuse them
in this notion.

00:07:00.185 --> 00:07:01.854
You've done better work.

00:07:01.854 --> 00:07:03.722
-Better work.
-Yeah.

00:07:03.722 --> 00:07:06.559
-During lockdown,
we all do things --

00:07:06.559 --> 00:07:07.793
There was a point
where I thought,

00:07:07.793 --> 00:07:09.595
"Maybe one day, I'll have
to delete all of this,"

00:07:09.595 --> 00:07:11.630
because we all went mad
in lockdown,

00:07:11.630 --> 00:07:13.465
and maybe we don't want
the evidence of what we did

00:07:13.465 --> 00:07:14.767
in lockdown out there.

00:07:14.767 --> 00:07:17.603
But then I'm thinking,
"No, it's part of my art."

00:07:17.603 --> 00:07:21.673
During lockdown,
I made a 12-part reality TV show

00:07:21.673 --> 00:07:23.176
called "Lone Island"...
-Yeah.

00:07:23.176 --> 00:07:25.877
-...about a man
who goes on dating show,

00:07:25.877 --> 00:07:30.216
but because of COVID,
no one else goes on with him.

00:07:30.216 --> 00:07:31.917
And he ends up falling in love
with a plant

00:07:31.917 --> 00:07:34.953
and a football and a mop.
[ Laughter ]

00:07:34.953 --> 00:07:37.155
And as the series went on,
my hair got longer.

00:07:37.155 --> 00:07:39.225
I looked -- I look madder.
-Here you go.

00:07:39.225 --> 00:07:41.059
This is, I guess,
on a date now with...

00:07:41.059 --> 00:07:42.828
-With ball.
-Yeah.

00:07:42.828 --> 00:07:46.398
-With ball,
and I got so into it,

00:07:46.398 --> 00:07:48.668
and I wrote, like,
a proper season arc.

00:07:48.668 --> 00:07:50.636
12-part season arc.
It's like "Ted Lasso."

00:07:50.636 --> 00:07:52.671
At the beginning, you're like,
"I don't know if I like plant,"

00:07:52.671 --> 00:07:54.941
and in the end, you're like,
"Plant had their reasons."

00:07:54.941 --> 00:07:58.043
[ Laughter ]

00:07:58.043 --> 00:08:01.580
And I remember, like,
editing the finale --

00:08:01.580 --> 00:08:03.215
the season finale,
and I was crying,

00:08:03.215 --> 00:08:05.384
and I was like,
"You have lost your damn mind."

00:08:05.384 --> 00:08:06.952
[ Laughter ]

00:08:06.952 --> 00:08:09.688
-Well, that's good.
I think a lot of people --

00:08:09.688 --> 00:08:11.056
you know, "Ted Lasso,"
season two,

00:08:11.056 --> 00:08:12.390
is coming to a close.

00:08:12.390 --> 00:08:14.960
There's gonna obviously
be a gap until season three.

00:08:14.960 --> 00:08:17.696
I think anybody
could go find "Lone Island"...

00:08:17.696 --> 00:08:19.097
-Yeah.
-...and fill that gap.

00:08:19.097 --> 00:08:21.733
-And have me sectioned, I think.
[ Laughter ]

00:08:21.733 --> 00:08:23.735
-Hey, it's really a pleasure
to meet you.

00:08:23.735 --> 00:08:25.671
Congratulations on everything.
-Thank you for having me.

00:08:25.671 --> 00:08:27.172
-Thank you.
-I appreciate it.

00:08:27.172 --> 00:08:29.375
-The second season finale
of "Ted lasso" is available

00:08:29.375 --> 00:08:31.377
to stream this Friday
on Apple TV+.

